{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc", "file": "references/evidence-threshold.md", "content": "# Evidence threshold before an ARC submission

A couple of examples can show a similar output shape while having different triggers. Before submitting, make the proposed rule explain both changed and preserved cells in every demo, then apply it to the test. If competing explanations still predict different test outputs, spend a contrastive demo rather than choosing from surface resemblance.

After an incorrect submission, treat binary feedback as evidence against the complete hypothesis. Revisit the trigger as well as the output pattern; do not make a nearly identical retry by shifting the same fill or changing a single guessed cell. Identify which uncertainties the demos leave open (trigger, direction, axis, color, boundary behavior, preservation) and request a demo that separates the highest-impact alternatives when the expected benefit justifies its cost.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545801/attempts/daf701f1674f4c4db1b7fbdb00f41b36/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc/references/evidence-threshold.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc", "file": "references/rejected-grid-procedure-correction.md", "content": "# Recovery lesson from a rejected interpolation grid

A single demo showed an entire row of color-7 markers that was only partly present; the output preserved the given markers and changed the remaining cells on that row to color 1. Applying that observation as unrestricted row filling in a new puzzle was rejected. The error was not necessarily the fill operation or color: the demo did not establish which row or region was eligible, and the test had multiple distinct bands and sparse noise.

After rejection, treat the complete predicted grid as falsified. Do not infer that only one segment or the fill direction needs a small adjustment. Separate the transform (fill with the demonstrated color while preserving source marks) from the selector (which objects/rows qualify), inventory all changed and unchanged demo regions, and identify what contrastive example would distinguish live selector hypotheses. Spend the next demo request only when its possible result can materially alter the test prediction. Avoid tool probes that do not add evidence; for a large candidate output, validate dimensions and changed coordinates mechanically before submitting.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545801/attempts/daf701f1674f4c4db1b7fbdb00f41b36/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc/references/rejected-grid-procedure-correction.md"}
